<attribute name="presentationName" nodeId="eaa3c23">Perform change stakeholder analysis</attribute>
<attribute name="briefDescription" nodeId="c1d13864"></attribute>
<attribute name="suppressed" nodeId="f91c33e5">false</attribute>
<attribute name="orderingGuide" nodeId="11b59b85"></attribute>
<attribute name="authors" nodeId="a59d2ed8"></attribute>
<attribute name="changeDate" nodeId="b868954a">Mon Jul 27 12:11:27 EDT 2015</attribute>
<attribute name="changeDescription" nodeId="e94549b3"></attribute>
<attribute name="version" nodeId="63d307a4"></attribute>
<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="fbe25f27">&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Conduct high-level stakeholder segmentation.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Validate stakeholder segments with key internal team members such as the central communications team, leadership
        team members, and business engagement teams.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Conduct stakeholder analysis in order to: 
        &lt;ul&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                Identify level of stakeholder commitment
            &lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                Identify level of stakeholder influence and support
            &lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                Identify stakeholder requirements from the programme
            &lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                Identify programme requirements from the respective stakeholders
            &lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Develop a detailed stakeholder map to plot all stakeholder segments for ease of analysis and engagement planning.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Discuss and validate the stakeholder analysis findings with key programme team members and programme leadership
        members (if required).
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="50a397fb"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="a90dc8ca"></attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="70b6c244"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="31cc0f5c">To enable the creation of a plan for managing stakeholders through the change process – their expectations, knowledge,
skills and experience. Engaging stakeholders (people impacted or needing to be engaged in order for the change initiative
to meet stated objectives) is done to build two way dialogue with program members, change sponsors and business managers.
Creating channels for open/honest communications is important for the program team and business to identify and address
issues in a proactive way to prevent people related implementation risk. To create these channels or engagement events the
stakeholder population needs to be identified and segmented by their differences and similarities in how they may be
impacted or react to change.</attribute>
